Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 10:41:58 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Updated mapping: hand-picked banks get their own provenance
 (mapped_by_hand), shown as a tab on the Outputs step

Approving the pipeline's suggestion in review and picking a bank for an
unmatched filer used to share one _source (reviewed_approved), so the
Outputs step could not show which rows were mapped by hand. apply_decisions
now tags decisions whose method starts with "Manual" as mapped_by_hand,
keeps by_source in the run summary after an Add, and the provenance table
re-reads when the run's updated-mapping file changes. The Add message says
how many went in by hand vs approved in review.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K5M7FnXPWrv7D7XYUXLqa1
